    <h2 class="section-title">Why 1099 Contractors Face Tax Problems</h2>
    <div class="service-content-full">
      <p>Unlike W-2 employees, 1099 contractors receive their full payment with no taxes withheld. This feels great until tax time when you realize you owe thousands you didn't set aside. Add the 15.3% self-employment tax on top of income tax, and many contractors find themselves in serious debt.</p>
      <p>The good news? An IRS Installment Agreement lets you pay your tax debt in monthly payments over time. It's the most common way to resolve tax debt, and it's much easier to qualify for than an Offer in Compromise.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

